From d527ee56fa4c9161ff59b94f8555a91598121c4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:34:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] XHCI X2: command ring engine + event producer

Doorbell 0 walks the command ring under the consumer discipline
measured from the AuraLite-OS xHCI driver (xhci.c:824-1010): Cycle-bit
ownership, Link TRBs flipping the consumer cycle on TC, completion
code read from Status[31:24] (the guest's control field), slot id
from Control[31:24]. No Op (23) completes with the command TRB's
physical address echoed as the event Parameter; Enable Slot (9)
allocates the first free id under the CONFIG.MaxSlotsEn gate and
Disable Slot (10) frees it; every other command (the X3 set) is
refused with cc 5 and the ring keeps working. Refusal codes are the
spec values the guest does not branch on beyond cc==1: 9 No Slots
Available, 11 Slot Not Enabled, 5 TRB Error (slot 0/>32, unknown).
Completion is synchronous at doorbell time (the guest polls the event
ring after ringing, XHCI_PLAN 1a) so runs stay deterministic.

The event-ring producer walks the ERST from guest memory and tracks
producer/consumer as absolute counts (the producer cycle of event n
derives from n); a full ring drops rather than overwrites. Posting
latches IMAN.IP, USBSTS.EINT mirrors it, ERDP reads back with EHB set
while an event is unacknowledged, and an ERDP write advances the
consumer mirror while its EHB write-1 clears the latch -- exactly the
consume discipline the guest performs after every event (its comment:
"QEMU tolerates omitting this; real silicon stops"). CRCR writes
restart the consumer (dequeue + RCS). The INTx pin itself is driven
in X5.

tests/test_xhci.c gains four groups: the No Op round-trip with the
IP/EINT/EHB latch cycle; the guest's own U1 gate re-hosted -- 256/256
No Ops across a Link wrap with exact Parameter echoes and producer
cycles; slot alloc/free/reuse with the measured refusal codes; and
the honest edges (X3 refusal, unowned TRB untouched, doorbell while
stopped queues until RUN). NC: src/xhci.c reverted to X1 -> 24
failures across the X2 groups. Gates: make test, make test-sanitize,
both SeaBIOS ISO lanes green.

Also repairs the XHCI_PLAN status line, which a same-file edit race
left at "X1 queued" in 0077 while the phase table and section 1e
already recorded X1 done.

tests/fpu_payload.elf stays untracked (a generated F4 gate artifact).
